    m_Localized: Constantinople
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037675
    m_Localized: An oasis on the northern route across the Taklamakan. Caravans stock
      up on water before crossing the desert.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037676
    m_Localized: One of the world's oldest bazaars. Caravans from east and west meet
      beneath the stone vaults of the covered market.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037677
    m_Localized: Sacred confluence of the Ganges and Yamuna. Pilgrims from across
      India come to bathe in the holy waters.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037678
    m_Localized: A fortress at the crossroads of worlds. Crusaders and Muslims fought
      for centuries over control of this coast.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037679
    m_Localized: The last Chinese outpost. Beyond its walls lies the endless desert
      and the lands of nomads.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037680
    m_Localized: A dusty port on the Red Sea shore. Pilgrims embark from here to
      the holy cities of Arabia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037681
    m_Localized: The Round City on the Tigris. The House of Wisdom holds the knowledge
      of the entire world. The Caliph rules from his golden palace.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037682
    m_Localized: "Mother of cities \u2014 the oldest city in Central Asia. Lapis
      lazuli is mined and cotton grown here."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037683
    m_Localized: A city of scholars and artisans. Bukhara's madrasas are renowned
      across the Muslim world. Its masters weave the finest carpets.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037684
    m_Localized: Capital of the Mamluks at the foot of the pyramids. The Nile carries
      Africa's wealth through the greatest bazaar of the East.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665172037685
    m_Localized: "The port of Gujarat \u2014 India's trading window to Arabia and
      Africa. Textiles and spices head westward."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231936
    m_Localized: The end of the Silk Road. The dome of Hagia Sophia is visible for
      miles. The Walls of Theodosius are impregnable. Here East meets West.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231937
    m_Localized: The oldest continuously inhabited city. Damascus steel and silk
      are prized from China to Europe.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231938
    m_Localized: Capital of the Delhi Sultanate. Its vast market and immeasurable
      riches attract merchants from across Asia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231939
    m_Localized: The Mogao Caves hold thousands of Buddhist frescoes. Pilgrims and
      merchants pray here before the perilous crossing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231940
    m_Localized: A trading town on the road from the Levant to Egypt. The last stop
      before the Sinai Desert.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231941
    m_Localized: An island fortress in the Persian Gulf. All sea routes between India
      and Persia pass through this port.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231942
    m_Localized: A caravan stop in the narrow Hexi Corridor between mountains and
      desert. Water skins are filled here for the long road ahead.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231943
    m_Localized: A mountain pass between worlds. The road from Central Asia to India
      runs through this harsh frontier city.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231944
    m_Localized: "The great crossroads \u2014 here the northern and southern routes
      around the Taklamakan converge. The road west lies open."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231945
    m_Localized: City of jade and silk on the southern route. Stones from the Yurunkash
      riverbanks are worth their weight in gold in Beijing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231946
    m_Localized: An ancient Buddhist center on the northern route. Monastery ruins
      recall its former grandeur.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231947
    m_Localized: Sacred city on the roof of the world. The Potala Palace towers above
      the valley. Monks preserve ancient wisdom.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231948
    m_Localized: Mountain city of the Naxi people. Tea and horses are the main goods
      on the ancient Tea Horse Road.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231949
    m_Localized: A city on the road from Central Asia to Persia. Caravans rest here
      after crossing the mountains.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231950
    m_Localized: The holiest site of Islam. Millions of pilgrims from around the
      world flock to the Kaaba. Trade thrives during the Hajj season.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231951
    m_Localized: City of the Prophet. The second holiest city of Islam. Pilgrims
      come to pay respects at the Prophet's Mosque.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231952
    m_Localized: An oasis in the Karakum Desert. An ancient fortress and military
      garrison control the trade routes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231953
    m_Localized: A city on the Tigris opposite the ruins of Nineveh. A strategic
      crossing between Mesopotamia and the Levant.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231954
    m_Localized: City of turquoise mines and poetry. Birthplace of Omar Khayyam.
      Caravans carry precious stones from here.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231955
    m_Localized: "The Fergana Valley \u2014 fertile lands at the gateway to Central
      Asia. Fruits and cotton abound here."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231956
    m_Localized: A city on the banks of the Ganges. River trade brings goods from
      deep within India.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231957
    m_Localized: An ancient city at the foot of the Alborz. The ruins of Rey hold
      memories of millennia of trade.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231958
    m_Localized: Heart of the Silk Road. Registan Square gleams with mosaics. Merchants
      from around the world trade at the great bazaar.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231959
    m_Localized: "An Omani port \u2014 the starting point for voyages to India. Dhows
      laden with goods depart with the monsoon winds."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231960
    m_Localized: A trade hub between Persia and Anatolia. Tabriz Bazaar is one of
      the largest covered markets in the world.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231961
    m_Localized: A Bengali port on the route to the islands of Southeast Asia. Monsoons
      set the rhythm of trade.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231962
    m_Localized: A major Central Asian city near the Tien Shan mountains. Water from
      mountain rivers feeds gardens and fields.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231963
    m_Localized: "An ancient city of Gandhara \u2014 a crossroads of Greek and Indian
      cultures. University ruins hold the wisdom of ages."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231964
    m_Localized: A Black Sea port at the foot of the mountains. Gateway to Anatolia
      for merchants from the Caucasus and Persia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231965
    m_Localized: A Levantine port with a Crusader fortress. Ships carry goods along
      the Mediterranean coast.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231966
    m_Localized: "An oasis in the Turfan Depression \u2014 the hottest place on the
      route. Grapes and melons grow amid the sands."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7217665176231967
    m_Localized: "The Jade Gate \u2014 China's ancient frontier. Beyond these gates
      the empire ends and the unknown begins."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7219978439745536
    m_Localized: Hami
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7219978485882880
    m_Localized: A desert oasis on the road from China westward. Caravans stop here
      to fill their water before the long crossing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9425860418330624
    m_Localized: Urumqi
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9425860468662272
    m_Localized: An oasis on the northern route along the Tian Shan. Caravans pass
      through here on the way to Kucha.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
